# ai-dev-sandbox — network allowlist.
#
# Baked into the image, root-owned, and NOT writable from inside the container.
#
# Changing it requires `ccnet rebuild`, which only the host can trigger — that is
# deliberate, so a sandboxed process cannot widen its own boundary. This file sits
# in the build context and is COPYd straight in, so no installer re-run is needed.
# (sandbox.conf is different: it is COMPILED into the generated Dockerfile, so a
# change there needs ./install.sh --project <project> before the rebuild.)
#
# `ccnet open` / `ccnet close` need no rebuild — they toggle the airlock against
# the list already baked in.
#
# api.anthropic.com is always permitted and must not be listed here; without it
# Claude cannot run at all.
#
# Two kinds of entry:
#
#   example.com      a domain. Reachable only while the airlock is OPEN.
#   tcp:host:port    an internal service. Reachable in BOTH modes, because an
#                    app must still reach its database while closed. Must
#                    resolve to a private address; a public one is refused.

# --- domains, reachable when OPEN -------------------------------------------

# Source control
github.com
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
objects.githubusercontent.com

# PHP / Composer
packagist.org
repo.packagist.org

# Node / npm / yarn
registry.npmjs.org
registry.yarnpkg.com

# Other registries — uncomment as needed
# pypi.org
# files.pythonhosted.org
# proxy.golang.org
# sum.golang.org
# crates.io
# static.crates.io

# Browser binaries for e2e suites — uncomment as needed. These are NOT
# registries: each is a postinstall script fetching a browser tarball, which is
# why allowlisting the registries alone still leaves `yarn install` failing on a
# project using Cypress or Puppeteer. The failure looks like a hang, not a
# refusal — a DROP surfaces as AggregateError/EHOSTUNREACH, so it reads as a
# proxy problem and sends you looking in the wrong place.
#
# Cypress app: download.cypress.io 302s to cdn.cypress.io, so both are needed.
# download.cypress.io
# cdn.cypress.io
# Chrome + chromedriver: puppeteer and chromedriver fetch binaries from Google
# storage and read their version index from googlechromelabs.
# storage.googleapis.com
# chromedriver.storage.googleapis.com
# googlechromelabs.github.io
#
# Note storage.googleapis.com resolves to ~11 addresses across many /24s and
# Google rotates them, so the /24 expansion is especially wide here and a stale
# ipset needs a re-run of `ccnet open` to re-resolve. Downloading a browser is
# also not the same as being able to run one: Chrome needs libnss3, libatk,
# libgbm and friends, which is a preset change, not an allowlist one.

# --- internal services, reachable in BOTH modes -----------------------------
tcp:db:3306
